  "status": "formal",
  "supportedClaim": "For unit phases and bounded observation coupling, replacing selected-root counting by the complete squared-slope mass changes the exact lattice factor from N M/K_s to M/K_s and the normalized envelope from M^-1 to M^-2. The same upper envelope becomes asymptotically M^-5/6 for eta=M^(1/2) and nonvanishing at eta=M^(6/7); a fixed window can lose launch enstrophy exponentially, while launch-inclusive payment has retention one by definition.",
  "takeaway": "For unit phases and bounded observation coupling, replacing selected-root counting by the complete squared-slope mass changes the exact lattice factor from N M/K_s to M/K_s and the normalized envelope from M^-1 to M^-2. The same upper envelope becomes asymptotically M^-5/6 for eta=M^(1/2) and nonvanishing at eta=M^(6/7); a fixed window can lose launch enstrophy exponentially, while launch-inclusive payment has retention one by definition."
